{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>as YHWH spoke by the hand of Moses to him</b> — like \"upon him,\" upon Korah. And what is the meaning of \"by the hand of Moses,\" and why did it not write \"to Moses\"? It is a hint to those who dispute the priesthood, that they are stricken with tzara'at just as Moses was stricken in his hand, and on this account Uzziah was stricken with tzara'at. According to its plain sense: he shall not be swallowed up or burned like Korah and his congregation, but rather as was done to Moses by his hand — he was stricken with tzara'at. And there are those who interpret: \"that no stranger who is not of the seed of Aaron draw near, as YHWH spoke by the hand of Moses to Aaron\" — that he and his sons shall be priests and no stranger — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 17:5). But the correct interpretation is that it alludes to Eleazar who was mentioned, as Scripture says: \"Speak to Eleazar son of Aaron\" etc. (Numbers 17:2), and its reading is: \"And Eleazar the priest took the copper firepans that the burned ones had brought, and they hammered them out as a plating for the altar, as YHWH spoke by the hand of Moses to him, as a memorial for the children of Israel\" etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:28.928853509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}